From c1888359451364f927006069d937563da0053db4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Page <744035+ben-page@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:05:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] winewayland: Let resizable windows be resized from just
 outside their edges.

Server-side decorations, and the client-side decorations of GTK and Qt,
take resize grabs a few pixels outside a window's edges as well as on
them. A Wine window can only be resized from inside its own surface, so
windows that draw their own frame, such as WPF windows using
WindowChrome, have a resize band only a few pixels wide.

Give resizable toplevels a transparent subsurface below them that reaches
8 surface units past their edges and takes pointer input only outside the
window. There the pointer shows resize cursors, through the cursor shape
protocol, and a press starts a compositor resize. It is left out for
maximized and fullscreen windows, where it would reach into other
monitors.

Whether the pointer is over the window or its border is decided from
where it is, not from which surface the compositor reports it on: after
a compositor move or resize, KWin keeps the pointer on whichever of the
window's surfaces it was on until the next click, as its seat never sees
the button release that ended the operation.
